   "note": "COLUMN COUNT AUDIT. Read at leaf 323 = printed p.317 (GAS-GAY) -- the exact anchor the CSV note cites. The offset checks out (+6) and the column count does NOT: the page is TWO columns, not the recorded 3. The note's claim that 'the 2->3 transition is 1857->1859' is therefore wrong; 1859 is still 2-column. The page also carries two conventions: '(col'd)' after a name as a race marker -- 'Gaskin Joseph (col'd), barber, h 41 Watts' -- which the project has documented for BROOKLYN (Hearne/Ogden '*', Hope & Henderson) but not for Manhattan Trow; and '(refused)' -- 'Gatty (refused), 169 Monroe' -- for a resident who declined to give information."
  }
